1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,620
If your old PC feels painfully slow, there's one upgrade that usually beats all the others.

2
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:10,383
Many older PCs still run on a hard drive.

3
00:00:10,663 --> 00:00:16,576
It stores data on spinning platters, read by an arm that has to physically move into place.

4
00:00:17,326 --> 00:00:18,192
That's slow.

5
00:00:18,472 --> 00:00:24,252
A typical hard drive reads around 150 to 200 megabytes per second.

6
00:00:25,002 --> 00:00:28,165
A solid state drive has no moving parts at all.

7
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:36,085
Even a basic one is several times faster, and an NVMe SSD can read thousands of megabytes per second.

8
00:00:36,835 --> 00:00:40,295
Boot times, app launches and loading screens all shrink.

9
00:00:40,575 --> 00:00:44,741
Before you buy anything else, check whether you're still on a hard drive.

10
00:00:45,021 --> 00:00:47,599
The full PC breakdown is on the channel.

